 07:42:06.160735+05:30	2026-10-18 00:12:01.808026+05:30	2026-10-18 07:42:06.170829+05:30	### Executive Intelligence Synthesis: Fisherman\n**Query:** Offshore wave monitoring near Malpe port\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Safety Status:** **🟢 SAFE FOR FISHING: ALL NEARSHORE & OFFSHORE CRAFT (0 - 20 NM)**\n- **Marine Forecast:** Significant wave height averages `0.61 m` (calm swell) with sea temperature at `30.75 °C` and current velocity of `0.07 m/s`. Douglas Sea State: Class 2-3 (Smooth / Slight).\n- **Operational Guidance & What to Do:**\n  1. Motorized craft, gillnetters, and trawlers from Mangaluru, Ullal, Malpe, and Karwar may operate normally.\n  2. Optimal departure windows: Early morning (04:00 - 10:00 IST) and late evening with calm nearshore currents.\n  3. Standard VHF Channel 16 watch advised. No active tropical cyclones, depressions, or squall warnings in the Arabian Sea.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.75  °C (range: 30.5 - 31.1  °C across 168 forecast hours). `30.75 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 0.61 m (median: 0.62 m, range: 0.48 - 0.66 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.07 m/s (peak: 0.22 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** Estimated 174,106 residents across 4 coastal settlement(s) (Udupi City Municipality, Padubidri Coastal Village, Kaup (Kapu) Coastal Town, Brahmavar-Barkur Coastal Node) fall within the hazard footprint. `174,106 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** 1 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: Malpe Fishing Harbour. `1 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #6]** 1 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Government Hospital, Udupi. `1 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #7]** 1 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: St. Mary's Islands Geo-Heritage Site. `1 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #8]** Live ocean observation at (13.35°N, 74.70°E) records significant wave height of 0.62 m (swell height 0.52 m, wave period 9.4 s, wind wave 0.04 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 9\n- **Primary Data Sources:** Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 8 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- Population figures reflect official Census counts and do not account for real-time transient, tourist, or floating populations.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_6f0c13b468: 8/8 claims matched, 57 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-sst-11a68981", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calcul