ents": ["coastal_risk", "ocean_research", "marine_hazard", "evidence_verification"], "verification_required": true, "created_at": "2026-10-17T19:20:19.142449Z"}	2026-10-18 00:50:23.670463+05:30	2026-10-18 00:50:23.680585+05:30	2026-10-18 05:17:38.704291+05:30	### Executive Intelligence Synthesis: Fisherman\n**Query:** I am planning to fish offshore near Mangaluru tomorrow morning. Investigate wave and wind forecasts and any active cyclone warnings.\n\n#### 1. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka °Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.76 °°C (range: 30.6 - 31.0 °°C across 168 forecast hours). `30.76 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka °Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 0.68 m (median: 0.68 m, range: 0.56 - 0.72 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka °Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.09 m/s (peak: 0.17 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** Estimated 624,301 residents across 5 coastal settlement(s) (Mangaluru °City °Corporation, Ullal °Coastal Municipality, Surathkal °Coastal Settlement, Padubidri °Coastal Village and 1 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `624,301 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** 2 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: New Mangalore Port (NMPT), Old Mangalore Port (Bunder). `2 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #6]** 1 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Wenlock Hospital, Mangaluru. `1 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #7]** 1 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Netravati-Gurupura Estuarine Mangroves. `1 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #8]** Live ocean observation at (12.91°N, 74.86°E) records significant wave height of 0.72 m (swell height 0.64 m, wave period 9.2 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: NEEDS_REVIEW)*\n- **[Finding #9]** Historical precedent: Extremely Severe °Cyclonic Storm Tauktae (2021) produced peak observed waves of 5.8 m and gusts of 85 km/h, impacting Ullal, Mangaluru Bengre Spit, Malpe. *(Status: NEEDS_REVIEW)*\n- **[Finding #10]** Historical precedent: Very Severe °Cyclonic Storm Ockhi (2017) produced peak observed waves of 4.5 m and gusts of 65 km/h, impacting Mangaluru Bunder, Ullal, Someshwara. *(Status: NEEDS_REVIEW)*\n\n#### 2. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 13\n- **Primary Data Sources:** India Meteorological Department (IMD) & INCOIS, Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n\n#### 3. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 7 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 3 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 4. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- Population figures reflect official Census counts and do not account for real-time transient, tourist, or floating populations.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_e06060a1a7: 7/10 claims matched, 69 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "fin