s: evaluate weekly tidal swell impact and coastal erosion exposure within 50km of Uttara Kannada (Karwar).\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Maritime Traffic & Port Clearance:** **🟢 NORMAL NAVIGATION / PORTS OPERATIONAL**\n- **Hydrodynamic Regime:** Calm wave regime (`0.68 m`). Coastal navigation channels open without draft restrictions.\n- **Actionable Directives & What to Do:**\n  1. New Mangalore Deep Port, Karwar Port, and Malpe Harbour operating at full commercial clearance.\n  2. Coastal infrastructure within 30km hazard buffer remains under zero-risk conditions.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Estimated 170,910 residents across 6 coastal settlement(s) (Murudeshwar Coastal Town, Honnavar Town Municipality, Kumta Coastal Municipality, Gokarna Coastal Heritage Town and 2 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `170,910 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** 5 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: Honnavar Port & Estuary Terminal, Tadadi Commercial Fishing Port, Belekeri Natural Port, INS Kadamba / Karwar Naval Base (Project Seabird), Karwar Commercial Port (Baithkol). `5 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** 1 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Civil Hospital, Karwar. `1 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** 3 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Sharavati Estuary Mangrove Reserve, Aghanashini Estuary (Ramsar Wetland Site), Kali River Estuary & Mangrove Reserve. `3 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** Live ocean observation at (14.50°N, 74.35°E) records significant wave height of 0.68 m (swell height 0.58 m, wave period 9.7 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 16\n- **Primary Data Sources:** Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n- **Sample Cryptographic Hash:** `a28db3971128bb4a...` (SHA-256 Verified)\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 5 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- Population figures reflect official Census counts and do not account for real-time transient, tourist, or floating populations.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_f9646c4e86: 5/5 claims matched, 38 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_eba8845b_1", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_murudeshwar", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_honnavar", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_kumta", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_gokarna", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_ankola", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_karwar"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_eba8845b_2", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar_port_honnavar", "evi_cf_cf_kar_port_tadadi", "evi_cf_cf_kar_port_belekeri", "evi_cf_cf_kar_infra_kadamba_naval_base", "evi_cf_cf_kar_port_karwar"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_eba8845b_3", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf