 Significant wave height averages `0.69 m` (calm swell) with sea temperature at `30.75 °C` and current velocity of `0.08 m/s`. Douglas Sea State: Class 2-3 (Smooth / Slight).\n- **Operational Guidance & What to Do:**\n  1. Motorized craft, gillnetters, and trawlers from Mangaluru, Ullal, Malpe, and Karwar may operate normally.\n  2. Optimal departure windows: Early morning (04:00 - 10:00 IST) and late evening with calm nearshore currents.\n  3. Standard VHF Channel 16 watch advised. No active tropical cyclones, depressions, or squall warnings in the Arabian Sea.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.75  °C (range: 30.6 - 31.0  °C across 168 forecast hours). `30.75 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 0.69 m (median: 0.7 m, range: 0.54 - 0.78 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.08 m/s (peak: 0.19 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 1\n- **Primary Data Sources:** Open-Meteo Marine API\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 3 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_3ecd7e7d81: 3/3 claims matched, 21 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-sst-757ccd49", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-e615b30df8"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-wave-fb4a43c7", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-e615b30df8"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-current-99b81091", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-e615b30df8"]}], "overall_status": "verified", "investigation_id": "inv_1c96d3b4", "flagged_findings_count": 0, "verified_findings_count": 3, "unverified_findings_count": 0}	["Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.", "Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.", "Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements."]	[]	[{"hash": null, "unit": "°C, m, s, deg, m/s", "units": {"marine_wave_current_series": "°C, m, s, deg, m/s"}, "value": {"sample_count": 168}, "latitude": 12.87, "raw_data": {"value": {"sample_count": 168}}, "data_type": "marine_wave_current_series", "longitude": 74.88, "source_url": "https://marine-api.open-meteo.com/v1/marine?latitude=12.87&longitude=74.88", "evidence_id": "ev-om-live-e615b30df8", "source_name": "Open-Meteo Marine API", "retrieval_time": "2026-10-18T03:26:13.223788+00:00", "dataset_metadata": {"