onds": 25.0, "max_retries": 1}], "selected_agents": ["ocean_research", "coastal_risk", "marine_hazard", "evidence_verification"], "verification_required": true, "created_at": "2026-10-18T06:46:42.512320Z"}	2026-10-18 12:16:47.863081+05:30	2026-10-18 12:16:47.89338+05:30	2026-10-18 12:16:47.89338+05:30	### Executive Intelligence Synthesis: Coastal-Authority\n**Query:** Historical cyclone surge: simulate Extreme Cyclone Tauktae (5.8m waves) regional disaster inundation cone across entire 320km Karnataka coastline.\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Assessment:** 🚨 Simulated Extreme Cyclone Tauktae (5.8 m wave heights) inundation cone spans the full 320 km Karnataka coastline, threatening >1.07 million residents, 9 ports, 3 hospitals, and 5 key ecological habitats.\n- **Telemetry:** Sea‑surface temperature 30.17 °C (range 29.8‑30.7 °C); model mean significant wave height 0.72 m (median 0.74 m, range 0.62‑0.8 m); peak current velocity 0.36 m/s (mean 0.15 m/s); live observation at 13.85°N 74.50°E shows SWH 0.72 m, swell 0.50 m, period 9.5 s.\n- **Action 1:** Initiate immediate, phased evacuation of the 1,075,668 residents within the hazard footprint, prioritizing high‑density settlements (Mangaluru, Udupi, Karwar) and coordinating transport via road and maritime assets.\n- **Action 2:** Mobilize emergency resources to protect critical infrastructure: pre‑position sandbags, pumps, and rescue vessels at the 9 affected ports; activate surge protection and medical surge capacity at the 3 district hospitals; and deploy rapid‑response teams to safeguard the 5 ecological sites.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.17  °C (range: 29.8 - 30.7  °C across 168 forecast hours). `30.17 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 0.72 m (median: 0.74 m, range: 0.62 - 0.8 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.15 m/s (peak: 0.36 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** Estimated 1,075,668 residents across 19 coastal settlement(s) (Mangaluru City Corporation, Ullal Coastal Municipality, Surathkal Coastal Settlement, Udupi City Municipality and 15 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `1,075,668 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** 9 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: New Mangalore Port (NMPT), Old Mangalore Port (Bunder), Malpe Fishing Harbour, Bhatkal Fishing Port, Honnavar Port & Estuary Terminal, Tadadi Commercial Fishing Port, Belekeri Natural Port, INS Kadamba / Karwar Naval Base (Project Seabird), Karwar Commercial Port (Baithkol). `9 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #6]** 3 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Wenlock Hospital, Mangaluru, District Government Hospital, Udupi, District Civil Hospital, Karwar. `3 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #7]** 5 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Netravati-Gurupura Estuarine Mangroves, St. Mary's Islands Geo-Heritage Site, Sharavati Estuary Mangrove Reserve, Aghanashini Estuary (Ramsar Wetland Site), Kali River Estuary & Mangrove Reserve. `5 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #8]** Live ocean observation at (13.85°N, 74.50°E) records significant wave height of 0.72 m (swell height 0.50 m, wave period 9.5 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #9]** Historical precedent: Extremely Severe Cyclonic Storm Tauktae (2021) produced peak observed waves of 5.8 m and gusts of 85 km/h, impacting Ullal, Mangaluru Bengre Spit, Malpe. *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #10]** Historical precedent: Very Severe Cyclonic Storm Ockhi (2017) produced peak observed waves of 4.5 m and gusts of 65 km/h, impacting Mangaluru Bunder, Ullal, Someshwara. *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 40\n- **Primary Data Sources:** India Meteorological Department (IMD) & INCOIS, Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 10 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Shared marine database repository is not configured. Offline sample fixture was not substituted in production mode; current forecast was not substituted for missing historical data.\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_77b42e60b2: 10/10 claims matched, 74 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-sst-11d6c3eb", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-c4578d4e50"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-wave-69648e60", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation"