Verdict:** 🟢 Draft restrictions and approach safety are currently within acceptable limits given modest wave conditions.\n- **Metrics:** Significant wave height = 0.68 m (swell = 0.48 m, period = 9 s); hazard footprint includes 764,707 residents and 3 ports (New Mangalore Port, Old Mangalore Port, Malpe Fishing Harbour).\n- **Action 1:** Verify commercial vessel drafts against the published minimum depths for NMPT, Bunder, and Malpe Harbour; if draft exceeds clearance, request tide‑dependent scheduling or lightering.\n- **Action 2:** Implement reduced approach speeds and enhanced pilot monitoring for vessels entering the ports, especially under any increase in wave height or period beyond the observed 0.68 m/9 s baseline.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Estimated 764,707 residents across 7 coastal settlement(s) (Mangaluru City Corporation, Ullal Coastal Municipality, Surathkal Coastal Settlement, Udupi City Municipality and 3 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `764,707 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** 3 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: New Mangalore Port (NMPT), Old Mangalore Port (Bunder), Malpe Fishing Harbour. `3 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** 2 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Wenlock Hospital, Mangaluru, District Government Hospital, Udupi. `2 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** 2 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Netravati-Gurupura Estuarine Mangroves, St. Mary's Islands Geo-Heritage Site. `2 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** Live ocean observation at (12.91°N, 74.84°E) records significant wave height of 0.68 m (swell height 0.48 m, wave period 9.0 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 15\n- **Primary Data Sources:** Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n- **Sample Cryptographic Hash:** `d3a5cd0a81f1354b...` (SHA-256 Verified)\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 5 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- Population figures reflect official Census counts and do not account for real-time transient, tourist, or floating populations.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_3d0f15064e: 5/5 claims matched, 39 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_a7cc317e_1", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_mangaluru", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_ullal", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_surathkal", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_udupi", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_padubidri", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_kaup", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_mulki"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_a7cc317e_2", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar_port_nmpt", "evi_cf_cf_kar_port_old_mangaluru", "evi_cf_cf_kar_port_malpe"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_a7cc317e_3", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar