stal_risk", "evidence_verification"], "verification_required": true, "created_at": "2026-10-18T07:10:03.947539Z"}	2026-10-18 12:40:20.221373+05:30	2026-10-18 12:40:20.231358+05:30	2026-10-18 12:40:20.232357+05:30	### Executive Intelligence Synthesis: Disaster Management\n**Query:** Cyclone Tauktae wave surge and coastal population exposure across Dakshina Kannada and Udupi\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Assessment:** 🟢 Cyclone Tauktae’s surge and wave impacts are moderate; hazard footprint covers key coastal settlements but wave heights remain below 1 m.\n- **Metrics:** Mean sea‑surface temperature 30.31 °C (range 29.9‑31.1 °C); mean significant wave height 0.87 m (median 0.88 m, range 0.76‑0.94 m); mean current 0.12 m/s (peak 0.22 m/s); 913,358 residents across 13 settlements exposed; 4 ports, 2 hospitals, and 2 ecological sites within zone.\n- **Action 1:** Issue targeted coastal flood advisories for Mangaluru, Ullal, Surathkal, Udupi and surrounding villages; activate evacuation protocols for low‑lying zones and ensure shelters are stocked.\n- **Action 2:** Deploy rapid response teams to protect critical infrastructure (NMPT, Old Mangalore Port, Malpe and Bhatkal harbours) and health facilities; pre‑position sandbags and pump assets, and monitor real‑time wave/current observations for escalation.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.31  °C (range: 29.9 - 31.1  °C across 168 forecast hours). `30.31 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 0.87 m (median: 0.88 m, range: 0.76 - 0.94 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.12 m/s (peak: 0.22 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** Estimated 913,358 residents across 13 coastal settlement(s) (Mangaluru City Corporation, Ullal Coastal Municipality, Surathkal Coastal Settlement, Udupi City Municipality and 9 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `913,358 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** 4 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: New Mangalore Port (NMPT), Old Mangalore Port (Bunder), Malpe Fishing Harbour, Bhatkal Fishing Port. `4 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #6]** 2 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Wenlock Hospital, Mangaluru, District Government Hospital, Udupi. `2 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #7]** 2 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Netravati-Gurupura Estuarine Mangroves, St. Mary's Islands Geo-Heritage Site. `2 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #8]** Live ocean observation at (12.78°N, 74.50°E) records significant wave height of 0.84 m (swell height 0.60 m, wave period 9.7 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #9]** Historical precedent: Extremely Severe Cyclonic Storm Tauktae (2021) produced peak observed waves of 5.8 m and gusts of 85 km/h, impacting Ullal, Mangaluru Bengre Spit, Malpe. *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #10]** Historical precedent: Very Severe Cyclonic Storm Ockhi (2017) produced peak observed waves of 4.5 m and gusts of 65 km/h, impacting Mangaluru Bunder, Ullal, Someshwara. *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 25\n- **Primary Data Sources:** India Meteorological Department (IMD) & INCOIS, Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 10 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- Population figures reflect official Census counts and do not account for real-time transient, tourist, or floating populations.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_222fb92d44: 10/10 claims matched, 74 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-sst-25a0040d", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-bc9fc02d1e"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-wave-2eb9de09", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-bc9fc02d1e"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-current-24676fb5", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-bc9fc02d1e"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_328c3d95_1", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_mangaluru", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_ullal", "evi_cf