inv_4d726cf0	disaster_management	Cyclone Tauktae wave surge and coastal population exposure across Dakshina Kannada and Udupi	completed	{"plan_id": "plan_fa7ac299", "workspace": "disaster_management", "query": "Cyclone Tauktae wave surge and coastal population exposure across Dakshina Kannada and Udupi", "normalized_intent": "compound_disaster_coastal_exposure", "target_coordinates": {"latitude": 13.15, "longitude": 74.8, "radius_km": 120.0}, "target_time_horizon": "7-day numerical forecast + historical baseline", "steps": [{"step_id": "step_ocean_research", "agent_id": "ocean_research", "agent_name": "Ocean Intelligence & Research Agent", "phase": "specialist_concurrent", "dependencies": [], "description": "Analyze physical SST, thermal anomalies, currents, and biochemical chlorophyll-a spectra.", "timeout_seconds": 20.0, "max_retries": 2}, {"step_id": "step_marine_hazard", "agent_id": "marine_hazard", "agent_name": "Marine Hazard & Forecast Agent", "phase": "specialist_concurrent", "dependencies": [], "description": "Ingest storm track, Douglas sea state wave spectra, and meteorological alerts.", "timeout_seconds": 20.0, "max_retries": 2}, {"step_id": "step_coastal_risk", "agent_id": "coastal_risk", "agent_name": "Coastal Impact & Risk Agent", "phase": "specialist_dependent", "dependencies": ["step_marine_hazard"], "description": "Evaluate coastal settlement and population exposure using upstream hazard wave and surge parameters.", "timeout_seconds": 20.0, "max_retries": 2}, {"step_id": "step_evidence_verification", "agent_id": "evidence_verification", "agent_name": "Evidence & Scientific Verification Agent", "phase": "scientific_auditor", "dependencies": ["step_ocean_research", "step_marine_hazard", "step_coastal_risk"], "description": "Independently verify scientific claims, cryptographic SHA-256 evidence integrity, units, and detect cross-source conflicts.", "timeout_seconds": 25.0, "max_retries": 1}], "selected_agents": ["ocean_research", "marine_hazard", "coastal_risk", "evidence_verification"], "verification_required": true, "created_at": "2026-10-18T07:10:56.484381Z"}	2026-10-18 12:41:03.138171+05:30	2026-10-18 12:41:03.154093+05:30	2026-10-18 12:41:03.154093+05:30	### Executive Intelligence Synthesis: Disaster Management\n**Query:** Cyclone Tauktae wave surge and coastal population exposure across Dakshina Kannada and Udupi\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Assessment:** ⚠️ Moderate wave surge risk from Cyclone Tauktae affecting Dakshina Kannada and Udupi coastlines, with significant exposure of coastal populations and critical infrastructure.\n- **Metrics:** Mean sea‑surface temperature 30.72 °C; mean significant wave height 0.66 m (range 0.52‑0.72 m); mean current velocity 0.07 m/s (peak 0.17 m/s); ~913,358 residents across 13 settlements within the hazard footprint; 4 ports, 2 apex hospitals, and 2 key ecological sites intersect the zone.\n- **Action 1:** Issue immediate coastal flood and surge warnings; activate evacuation protocols for the 913 k residents, prioritizing low‑lying areas in Mangaluru, Ullal, Surathkal, and Udupi.\n- **Action 2:** Mobilize emergency response teams to safeguard New Mangalore Port, Old Mangalore Port, Malpe and Bhatkal harbours, and coordinate with District Wenlock Hospital and District Government Hospital for surge‑related medical preparedness.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.72  °C (range: 30.5 - 31.0  °C across 168 forecast hours). `30.72 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 0.66 m (median: 0.66 m, range: 0.52 - 0.72 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.07 m/s (peak: 0.17 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** Estimated 913,358 residents across 13 coastal settlement(s) (Mangaluru City Corporation, Ullal Coastal Municipality, Surathkal Coastal Settlement, Udupi City Municipality and 9 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `913,358 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** 4 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: New Mangalore Port (NMPT), Old Mangalore Port (Bunder), Malpe Fishing Harbour, Bhatkal Fishing Port. `4 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #6]** 2 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Wenlock Hospital, Mangaluru, District Government Hospital, Udupi. `2 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #7]** 2 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Netravati-Gurupura Estuarine Mangroves, St. Mary's Islands Geo-Heritage Site. `2 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #8]** Live ocean observation at (13.15°N, 74.80°E) records significant wave height of 0.66 m (swell height 0.54 m, wave period 9.2 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #9]** Historical precedent: Extremely Severe Cyclonic Storm Tauktae (2021) produced peak observed waves of 5.8 m and gusts of 85 km/h, impacting Ullal, Mangaluru Bengre Spit, Malpe. *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #10]** Historical precedent: Very Severe Cyclonic Storm Ockhi (2017) produced peak observed waves of 4.5 m and gusts of 65 km/h, impacting Mangaluru Bunder, Ullal, Someshwara. *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 25\n- **Primary Data Sources:** India Meteorological Department (IMD) & INCOIS, Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 10 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- Population figures reflect official Census counts and do not account for real-time transient, tourist, or floating populations.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_80148fbcff: 10/10 claims matched, 74 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-sst-55f7335c", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-c69b652806"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-wave-a0ef6e00", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-c69b652806"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-current-eb59ac7f", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["ev-om-live-c69b652806"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_4d726cf0_1", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_mangaluru", "evi_cf_cf_kar_s