ngaluru\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Verdict:** 🟢 Sea surface temperatures off Mangaluru remain elevated (average 30.75 °C, 30.6‑31.0 °C range) with no immediate thermal stress signals; chlorophyll‑a data are absent, so biological productivity cannot be directly quantified.\n- **Metrics:** Near‑surface SST forecast = 30.75 °C (mean); significant wave height = 0.69 m (median 0.7 m, range 0.54‑0.78 m); surface current velocity = 0.08 m/s (peak 0.19 m/s).\n- **What to Do 1:** Initiate near‑real‑time chlorophyll‑a monitoring using satellite ocean colour products (e.g., Sentinel‑3 OLCI) and validate with in‑situ fluorometer samples at key stations (e.g., 12.91°N, 74.85°E).\n- **What to Do 2:** Issue a fisheries advisory recommending heightened observation of plankton blooms and potential shifts in species distribution, leveraging the warm SST baseline and moderate wave conditions for proactive management.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.75  °C (range: 30.6 - 31.0  °C across 168 forecast hours). `30.75 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 0.69 m (median: 0.7 m, range: 0.54 - 0.78 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.08 m/s (peak: 0.19 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** Estimated 764,707 residents across 7 coastal settlement(s) (Mangaluru City Corporation, Ullal Coastal Municipality, Surathkal Coastal Settlement, Udupi City Municipality and 3 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `764,707 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** 3 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: New Mangalore Port (NMPT), Old Mangalore Port (Bunder), Malpe Fishing Harbour. `3 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #6]** 2 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Wenlock Hospital, Mangaluru, District Government Hospital, Udupi. `2 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #7]** 2 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Netravati-Gurupura Estuarine Mangroves, St. Mary's Islands Geo-Heritage Site. `2 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #8]** Live ocean observation at (12.91°N, 74.85°E) records significant wave height of 0.68 m (swell height 0.50 m, wave period 9.0 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 16\n- **Primary Data Sources:** Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 8 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Chlorophyll ocean-color measurements require satellite optical sensors (e.g. MODIS/Copernicus Sentinel-3). Not available in Open-Meteo meteorological feeds.\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_a631a2fd4e: 8/8 claims matched, 60 checks passed.", "details": 