angaluru\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Verdict:** 🟢 Sea surface temperature off Mangaluru is stable, averaging 30.65 °C (range 30.3‑31.1 °C); chlorophyll‑a data are absent, so biological productivity cannot be directly assessed.\n- **Metrics:** 168‑hour model forecasts show SST 30.65 °C, mean significant wave height 1.01 m (live buoy 0.96 m), and mean current velocity 0.16 m/s; no chlorophyll‑a observations recorded.\n- **Action 1:** Task satellite ocean‑colour sensors (e.g., Sentinel‑3 OLCI) to capture near‑real‑time chlorophyll‑a concentrations over the Mangaluru coastal zone and compare to historical baselines.\n- **Action 2:** Issue a fisheries advisory recommending monitoring of plankton shifts and adjusting port operations (NMPT, Old Mangalore) if temperature‑driven productivity changes are detected.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Near-surface sea temperature model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours averages 30.65  °C (range: 30.3 - 31.1  °C across 168 forecast hours). `30.65 °C` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** Wave model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean significant wave height of 1.01 m (median: 1.02 m, range: 0.94 - 1.1 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** Ocean current model forecast off Karnataka Coast across 168 forecast hours indicates mean current velocity of 0.16 m/s (peak: 0.31 m/s). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** Estimated 594,977 residents across 3 coastal settlement(s) (Mangaluru City Corporation, Ullal Coastal Municipality, Surathkal Coastal Settlement) fall within the hazard footprint. `594,977 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** 2 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: New Mangalore Port (NMPT), Old Mangalore Port (Bunder). `2 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #6]** 1 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Wenlock Hospital, Mangaluru. `1 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #7]** 1 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Netravati-Gurupura Estuarine Mangroves. `1 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #8]** Live ocean observation at (11.99°N, 74.47°E) records significant wave height of 0.96 m (swell height 0.76 m, wave period 10.2 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 9\n- **Primary Data Sources:** Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 8 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Chlorophyll ocean-color measurements require satellite optical sensors (e.g. MODIS/Copernicus Sentinel-3). Not available in Open-Meteo meteorological feeds.\n- Surface wind variables are not provided by Open-Meteo Marine API (marine-api.open-meteo.com); requires atmospheric weather API.\n- Chlorophyll observations are unavailable through Open-Meteo Marine API.\n- Open-Meteo values represent numerical model forecasts and estimates rather than direct in-situ buoy/sensor measurements.\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_e122a7cdbe: 8/8 claims matched, 58 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "fnd-live-sst-c7a3bbbf", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_i