inv_cba5284b	coastal-authority	7-day ocean conditions: evaluate weekly tidal swell impact and coastal erosion exposure within 50km of Uttara Kannada (Karwar).	completed	{"plan_id": "plan_128f2064", "workspace": "coastal-authority", "query": "7-day ocean conditions: evaluate weekly tidal swell impact and coastal erosion exposure within 50km of Uttara Kannada (Karwar).", "normalized_intent": "coastal_vulnerability_assessment", "target_coordinates": {"latitude": 14.5, "longitude": 74.35, "radius_km": 50.0}, "target_time_horizon": "7-day numerical forecast + historical baseline", "steps": [{"step_id": "step_marine_hazard", "agent_id": "marine_hazard", "agent_name": "Marine Hazard & Forecast Agent", "phase": "specialist_concurrent", "dependencies": [], "description": "Ingest storm track, Douglas sea state wave spectra, and meteorological alerts.", "timeout_seconds": 20.0, "max_retries": 2}, {"step_id": "step_coastal_risk", "agent_id": "coastal_risk", "agent_name": "Coastal Impact & Risk Agent", "phase": "specialist_dependent", "dependencies": ["step_marine_hazard"], "description": "Evaluate coastal settlement and population exposure using upstream hazard wave and surge parameters.", "timeout_seconds": 20.0, "max_retries": 2}, {"step_id": "step_evidence_verification", "agent_id": "evidence_verification", "agent_name": "Evidence & Scientific Verification Agent", "phase": "scientific_auditor", "dependencies": ["step_marine_hazard", "step_coastal_risk"], "description": "Independently verify scientific claims, cryptographic SHA-256 evidence integrity, units, and detect cross-source conflicts.", "timeout_seconds": 25.0, "max_retries": 1}], "selected_agents": ["coastal_risk", "marine_hazard", "evidence_verification"], "verification_required": true, "created_at": "2026-10-18T08:02:37.557795Z"}	2026-10-18 13:32:40.713742+05:30	2026-10-18 13:32:40.721639+05:30	2026-10-18 13:32:40.721639+05:30	### Executive Intelligence Synthesis: Coastal-Authority\n**Query:** 7-day ocean conditions: evaluate weekly tidal swell impact and coastal erosion exposure within 50km of Uttara Kannada (Karwar).\n\n#### 1. Operational Assessment & Decision Guidance\n- **Assessment:** ⚠️ Moderate tidal swell and erosion risk for the 50 km coastal zone around Karwar, affecting ~170,910 residents, five ports, and three critical estuarine habitats.\n- **Telemetry:** Live buoy at 14.50°N / 74.35°E reports significant wave height 0.66 m (swell 0.52 m, period 9.7 s); no wind‑generated wave component detected.\n- **Action:** Issue a 24‑hour coastal‑erosion advisory to municipal authorities (Karwar, Honnavar, Kumta, Gokarna) and port operators, urging temporary suspension of low‑lying shoreline activities and pre‑positioning of sand‑bag barriers at vulnerable stretches.\n- **Action:** Activate the District Civil Hospital’s emergency response plan and coordinate with the INS Kadamba naval base to deploy rapid‑response teams for real‑time shoreline monitoring and evacuation support if swell heights exceed 0.8 m.\n\n#### 2. Specialist Observations & Findings\n- **[Finding #1]** Estimated 170,910 residents across 6 coastal settlement(s) (Murudeshwar Coastal Town, Honnavar Town Municipality, Kumta Coastal Municipality, Gokarna Coastal Heritage Town and 2 others) fall within the hazard footprint. `170,910 people` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #2]** 5 maritime port/harbour facility(ies) intersect the hazard footprint: Honnavar Port & Estuary Terminal, Tadadi Commercial Fishing Port, Belekeri Natural Port, INS Kadamba / Karwar Naval Base (Project Seabird), Karwar Commercial Port (Baithkol). `5 ports` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #3]** 1 apex healthcare facility(ies) located within the hazard zone: District Civil Hospital, Karwar. `1 facilities` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #4]** 3 critical ecological habitat(s) intersect the hazard zone: Sharavati Estuary Mangrove Reserve, Aghanashini Estuary (Ramsar Wetland Site), Kali River Estuary & Mangrove Reserve. `3 habitats` *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n- **[Finding #5]** Live ocean observation at (14.50°N, 74.35°E) records significant wave height of 0.66 m (swell height 0.52 m, wave period 9.7 s, wind wave 0.00 m). *(Status: VERIFIED)*\n\n#### 3. Evidence Integrity & Cryptographic Provenance\n- **Total Evidence Records Ingested:** 16\n- **Primary Data Sources:** Open-Meteo Marine API, OpenStreetMap Contributors, Census of India & KSCZMA\n- **Sample Cryptographic Hash:** `a28db3971128bb4a...` (SHA-256 Verified)\n\n#### 4. Scientific Verification Audit\n- **Audit Status:** `VERIFIED`\n- **Verified Claims:** 5 | **Cross-Source Conflicts:** 0 | **Unverified:** 0\n\n#### 5. Operational Safety & Limitations\n- Proximity or polygon intersection indicates potential exposure, but does not model hydrodynamic inundation depth or wave force without local bathymetry and DEM data.\n- Population figures reflect official Census counts and do not account for real-time transient, tourist, or floating populations.\n- **Official Warning:** *This assessment provides supplementary computational intelligence and does not replace official meteorological advisories from the India Meteorological Department (IMD) or INCOIS.*	{"notes": "Scientific verification run vrun_c51a3c59a4: 5/5 claims matched, 38 checks passed.", "details": [{"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_cba5284b_1", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_murudeshwar", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_honnavar", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_kumta", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_gokarna", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_ankola", "evi_cf_cf_kar_settlement_karwar"]}, {"notes": "All applicable deterministic checks passed against verified source evidence.", "state": "verified", "finding_id": "f_coastal_inv_cba5284b_2", "missing_evidence_ids": [], "reproduced_calculation": null, "supporting_evidence_ids": ["e